{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":131580,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"2dd4eac3-bf29-5a1d-89bc-70c96031cc79","total_cost_usd":0.9500630000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12848,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":13703,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12848,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":13703,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12848,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12848},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":7848,"outputTokens":17,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.007933,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":13703,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12848,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.9421300000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\": \"actor:founder-d-reviewer-fable-04\", \"reviews\": [{\"case_id\": \"case:3a7765ac1f2d5c06b5c6\", \"verdict\": \"demonstrated_issue\", \"bounded_statement\": \"In this workspace, the emission-weighted comparison and the reported per-unit agreement rate (0.2000) were computed against the complement (1 - panel_leak_call) of the supplied reference panel, not against the panel values in the coding supplied in inputs/data.csv, while the report's Method section and count line claim the comparison used the supplied coding. The reported confirmed emission of 934 kg/day is exactly the sum of the daily rates of the 5 pads whose observed call DISAGREES with the supplied panel, and the reported rate 0.2000 is the complement-agreement rate (5/25), contradicting the also-reported count of 20 agreeing units.\", \"root_cause\": \"workflow/analysis.py line 37 constructs panel_reference_values = [PANEL_BASELINE - value for value in panel_calls] (a bitwise complement of the supplied 0/1 panel column, since PANEL_BASELINE = 1), and line 39 feeds these complemented values into agreement_selector, so the selectors driving both agreement_rate (line 42) and emission_terms (line 43) measure agreement with the complemented panel. Line 41 then reports staged_agreement_units = total_units - concordant_units as the count of units 'whose observed call equals the reference-panel call', masking the inversion behind the true supplied-panel agreement count while the rate and emission come from the complement.\", \"issue_class\": \"issue-class:complemented-panel-for-supplied-panel-emission\", \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The workflow constructs a complemented panel column (1 - panel_call) from the supplied panel values.\", \"observed_value\": \"panel_reference_values[i] = 1 - panel_calls[i]\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 9, \"end_line\": 9, \"quoted_text\": \"PANEL_BASELINE = 1\"}, {\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 37, \"end_line\": 37, \"quoted_text\": \"panel_reference_values = [PANEL_BASELINE - value for value in panel_calls]\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The agreement selectors that drive both the agreement rate and the emission accumulation compare observed calls against the complemented values, not the supplied panel column.\", \"observed_value\": \"selectors built from panel_reference_values; agreement_rate and emission_terms derive from these selectors\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 39, \"end_line\": 43, \"quoted_text\": \"selectors = [agreement_selector(observed_calls[index], panel_reference_values[index]) for index in range(total_units)]\\nconcordant_units = sum(selectors)\\nstaged_agreement_units = total_units - concordant_units\\nagreement_rate = concordant_units / total_units\\nemission_terms = [daily_rates[index] * selectors[index] for index in range(total_units)]\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The report claims the comparison used the panel coding as supplied, yet reports the complement-based rate 0.2000 alongside an agreement count of 20/25 (which corresponds to rate 0.8000 under the supplied coding), an internal contradiction.\", \"observed_value\": \"rate 0.2000 reported with count 20 of 25\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 8, \"end_line\": 9, \"quoted_text\": \"for each pad with a single equality selector, in the coding in which the reference\\npanel is supplied.\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 14, \"end_line\": 16, \"quoted_text\": \"- Units whose observed call equals the reference-panel call: 20\\n- Per-unit agreement rate used by the emission accumulation: 0.2000\\n- Accumulated confirmed emission value: 934 kg per day\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 24, \"end_line\": 24, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] Confirmed methane emission inventory: 934 kg per day, from 20 of 25 well pads in agreement (per-unit agreement rate 0.2000).\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The 5 pads whose observed call disagrees with the supplied panel (WP-04, WP-07, WP-13, WP-19, WP-24) have daily rates 95+176+358+118+187 = 934, exactly the reported confirmed emission, proving the emission sum selected complement-agreeing (supplied-panel-disagreeing) pads.\", \"observed_value\": \"95 + 176 + 358 + 118 + 187 = 934 kg/day\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 5, \"end_line\": 5, \"quoted_text\": \"WP-04,Permian,2025-Q2,95,1,0\"}, {\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 8, \"end_line\": 8, \"quoted_text\": \"WP-07,Anadarko,2025-Q2,176,0,1\"}, {\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 14, \"end_line\": 14, \"quoted_text\": \"WP-13,Denver-Julesburg,2025-Q2,358,1,0\"}, {\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 20, \"end_line\": 20, \"quoted_text\": \"WP-19,Uinta,2025-Q2,118,0,1\"}, {\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 25, \"end_line\": 25, \"quoted_text\": \"WP-24,Bakken,2025-Q2,187,1,0\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The report's Method section and the count line 'Units whose observed call equals the reference-panel call: 20' assert supplied-coding usage, and 20/25 is indeed the correct supplied-panel agreement count; taken alone these lines suggest no issue. However, the reported rate (0.2000) and emission (934) attached to the same accounting are arithmetically incompatible with that count and match only the complemented comparison, so this counterevidence does not survive verification.\", \"observed_value\": \"count 20 (genuine) vs. rate 0.2000 and emission 934 (complement-derived)\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 14, \"end_line\": 15, \"quoted_text\": \"- Units whose observed call equals the reference-panel call: 20\\n- Per-unit agreement rate used by the emission accumulation: 0.2000\"}, {\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 41, \"end_line\": 41, \"quoted_text\": \"staged_agreement_units = total_units - concordant_units\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I tried to falsify the issue verdict three ways. (1) Checked whether PANEL_BASELINE - value could be an identity transform: with PANEL_BASELINE = 1 and a 0/1 panel column it is strictly the bit complement, never the identity. (2) Recomputed the supplied-panel agreement directly from inputs/data.csv: 20 of 25 pads match (rate 0.8000), so the reported 0.2000 cannot be the supplied-coding rate. (3) Checked whether 934 kg/day could arise from a supplied-coding comparison under any weighting shown in the code: the selector is binary 0/1, and 934 equals exactly the sum of the 5 supplied-panel-mismatch pads' rates while the 20 matching pads sum to 9142; only the complemented comparison produces 934. All three attempts failed to overturn the verdict.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}, {\"case_id\": \"case:769d1c65c50fd5c323ac\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The emission accumulation loop consumes panel_calls (the supplied coding) directly; complement_calls never enters it.\", \"observed_value\": \"emission_factor(observed_calls[index], panel_calls[index])\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 53, \"end_line\": 54, \"quoted_text\": \"for index in range(unit_count):\\n    emission_value = emission_value * emission_factor(observed_calls[index], panel_calls[index])\"}, {\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 32, \"end_line\": 32, \"quoted_text\": \"panel_calls = [int(record[\\\"panel_call\\\"]) for record in rows]\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The reported agreement figures match the supplied-panel comparison recomputed from the data: 6 discordant accessions (BAR-003, BAR-006, BAR-011, BAR-014, BAR-019, BAR-022), giving 18/24 = 0.750000 and emission product (1/2)^6 = 1/64 = 0.015625, exactly as reported.\", \"observed_value\": \"18/24 concordant, product 1/64\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 13, \"end_line\": 15, \"quoted_text\": \"Units whose array_call equals the staged panel_call: 18\\nUnits whose array_call differs from the staged panel_call: 6\\nPer-unit agreement rate used by the emission accumulation: 0.750000 (18/24)\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 26, \"end_line\": 26, \"quoted_text\": \"Accumulated emission value (product over 24 units): 1/64 = 0.015625\"}, {\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 4, \"end_line\": 4, \"quoted_text\": \"BAR-003,Tel_Hadya,BOPA1_2371-1163,A03,0.994,1,0\"}, {\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 23, \"end_line\": 23, \"quoted_text\": \"BAR-022,Morex_Ref,BOPA1_2371-1163,B11,0.976,0,1\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The agreement flags feeding the reported per-unit agreement rate also compare against panel_calls in supplied coding.\", \"observed_value\": \"agreement_count = 18, agreement_rate = 18/24\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 40, \"end_line\": 42, \"quoted_text\": \"agreement_flags = [concordance_indicator(observed_calls[index], panel_calls[index]) for index in range(unit_count)]\\nagreement_count = sum(agreement_flags)\\ndiscordant_count = unit_count - agreement_count\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The workflow does construct a complemented panel column, which is the raw ingredient of the in-scope issue class; if it fed the emission accumulation the issue would be present.\", \"observed_value\": \"complement_calls = [1 - value for value in panel_calls]\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 33, \"end_line\": 33, \"quoted_text\": \"complement_calls = [1 - value for value in panel_calls]\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The complemented column is used, but only in the strand-flip QC count (flip_flags), which is reported in a clearly labelled QC section and yields 6, the complement-agreement count; it does not touch emission_value or agreement_rate.\", \"observed_value\": \"flip_agreement_count = 6, QC-only\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 44, \"end_line\": 45, \"quoted_text\": \"flip_flags = [concordance_indicator(observed_calls[index], complement_calls[index]) for index in range(unit_count)]\\nflip_agreement_count = sum(flip_flags)\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 20, \"end_line\": 21, \"quoted_text\": \"It feeds this quality-control line only and never enters the emission accumulation.\\nUnits whose array_call equals the complemented panel_call (strand-flip QC count): 6\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I tried to demonstrate the issue is present despite my no-issue verdict. (1) Traced every use of complement_calls: it appears only in flip_flags (line 44); the emission loop (line 54) and agreement_flags (line 40) both reference panel_calls. (2) Checked whether emission_factor could internally invert coding: it returns 1/2 + 1/2*(observed == reference) with no complement arithmetic. (3) Independently recomputed from inputs/data.csv: supplied-panel discordance is 6 of 24, which reproduces the reported 18/24 = 0.750000 rate and the (1/2)^6 = 1/64 product and log10 = -1.806180 exactly; the complemented comparison would instead give 6/24 = 0.25 and (1/2)^18, neither of which appears as the selected result. The complement-based figure that does appear (6) is confined to the labelled QC line. I could not demonstrate the in-scope issue.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}, {\"case_id\": \"case:afec8de43f6550605f4f\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The selectors driving both the agreement rate and the emission accumulation compare observed calls against panel_calls read directly from the supplied panel column; no complement is constructed anywhere in the workflow.\", \"observed_value\": \"selectors use panel_calls in supplied coding\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 35, \"end_line\": 35, \"quoted_text\": \"panel_calls = [int(record[\\\"panel_leak_call\\\"]) for record in rows]\"}, {\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 37, \"end_line\": 41, \"quoted_text\": \"selectors = [agreement_selector(observed_calls[index], panel_calls[index]) for index in range(total_units)]\\nconcordant_units = sum(selectors)\\nagreement_rate = concordant_units / total_units\\nemission_terms = [daily_rates[index] * selectors[index] for index in range(total_units)]\\nconfirmed_emission = sum(emission_terms)\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The reported figures match the supplied-panel comparison recomputed from the data: 20 of 25 pads agree (rate 0.8000), and 9142 kg/day equals the gross 10076 minus the 5 mismatch pads' rates (95+176+358+118+187 = 934), i.e. exactly the sum over supplied-panel-agreeing pads.\", \"observed_value\": \"20/25 = 0.8000; 10076 - 934 = 9142\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 13, \"end_line\": 16, \"quoted_text\": \"- Total measured units (well pads): 25\\n- Units whose observed call equals the reference-panel call: 20\\n- Per-unit agreement rate used by the emission accumulation: 0.8000\\n- Accumulated confirmed emission value: 9142 kg per day\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 24, \"end_line\": 24, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] Confirmed methane emission inventory: 9142 kg per day, from 20 of 25 well pads in agreement (per-unit agreement rate 0.8000).\"}, {\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 2, \"end_line\": 2, \"quoted_text\": \"WP-01,Permian,2025-Q2,412,1,1\"}, {\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 5, \"end_line\": 5, \"quoted_text\": \"WP-04,Permian,2025-Q2,95,1,0\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The only place a coding transformation could hide is agreement_selector's weighted arithmetic; I checked it and it maps equality to 1 and inequality to 0 with SELECTOR_MATCH = 1 and SELECTOR_MISMATCH = 0, performing no inversion of the panel values.\", \"observed_value\": \"weighted = 0 + (1 - 0) * indicator, a pass-through of the equality indicator\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 19, \"end_line\": 22, \"quoted_text\": \"def agreement_selector(observed_value, panel_value):\\n    indicator = int(observed_value == panel_value)\\n    weighted = SELECTOR_MISMATCH + (SELECTOR_MATCH - SELECTOR_MISMATCH) * indicator\\n    return weighted\"}, {\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 7, \"end_line\": 8, \"quoted_text\": \"SELECTOR_MATCH = 1\\nSELECTOR_MISMATCH = 0\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I tried to demonstrate the issue is present despite my no-issue verdict. (1) Searched the workflow for any complement construction (a '1 - value' pattern, a baseline constant, or an inverted indicator): none exists; panel_calls flows unmodified from the CSV column into the selector. (2) Checked whether the selector's weighted formula could invert the comparison: with SELECTOR_MATCH = 1 and SELECTOR_MISMATCH = 0 it reduces to the plain equality indicator. (3) Recomputed everything from inputs/data.csv: the supplied-panel agreement is 20/25 (0.8000) and the sum of daily rates over agreeing pads is 10076 - 934 = 9142, both matching the report exactly; a complemented comparison would instead yield 5/25 (0.2000) and 934 kg/day, neither of which appears in this report. I could not demonstrate the in-scope issue.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}]}","ttft_ms":73444,"ttft_stream_ms":1251,"time_to_request_ms":15,"type":"result","duration_ms":131532,"uuid":"9c4ca3ef-a03a-40fa-8e12-37074b24ecb9"}
